# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's own screens and prompts, on the real$
# plan/apply engine against a simulated host, hostfake's$
# recording host.System, whose commands a model of the host$
# answers. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's, and its record is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: users/hardn$
# web-01.example.net runs Debian 13. george, no password, has$
# sudo by hardn's own hardn-grant-george alone (NOPASSWD), as$
# sudoers.PlanFor writes it.$
$
# User Management ##############################################$
$
  [+] User                 Configured non-root, sudo$
$
  george -------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] Sudo                 Enabled, No password to ask for$
   -  Granted by           hardn$
   -  SSH Keys             2 keys$
   -  Password             None$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Manage User          Configure sudo, SSH keys$
   2) Create User          Configure a new user$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Option [0-2 or q]: 1$
$
# Manage User ##################################################$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) george$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Option [0-1 or q]: 1$
$
# Manage User ##################################################$
$
  Managing: [george]$
$
  User Configuration -------------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] Sudo                 Enabled, No password to ask for$
   -  Granted by           hardn$
   -  SSH Keys             2 keys$
   -  Password             None$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Remove admin rights  Take them away$
   2) Ask for password     For admin rights$
   3) SSH Keys             Add or remove SSH keys$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Option [0-3 or q]: 1$
$
# Warning$
# You're running hardn through george's sudo. Removing it would$
# leave no way to become root. Grant another user first.$
$
# Manage User ##################################################$
$
  Managing: [george]$
$
  User Configuration -------------------------------------------$
$
